---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseSection from "../../components/CaseSection.astro";
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex";
import { caseStudyStyles } from "../../styles/caseStudyStyles";
import { portfolioStyles } from "../../styles/portfolioStyles";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="XPO Event Chatbot | Warre Snaet"
  description="A full-stack event chatbot for Kortrijk Xpo Group, built with .NET, Azure OpenAI, Cosmos DB, Next.js, and Python ingestion."
  kicker="Academic team project for an external client, 2025"
  heading="Event chatbot for XPO Group"
  lead="An event assistant that answers visitor questions from exhibitor and event-site content. It also handles registration and collects usable analytics."
  meta={[
    { label: "My role", value: "Backend, retrieval, ingestion, integration, and deployment work" },
    { label: "Stack", value: ".NET, C#, Azure OpenAI, Cosmos DB, Next.js, Python, Scrapy" },
    { label: "Context", value: "Team project for Kortrijk Xpo Group" },
  ]}
>
  <CaseSection label="Problem" title="Answers from content that keeps changing">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>Visitors wanted quick answers about exhibitors, stands, and event details, and that information was spread over several event websites. The system had to collect the content, make it searchable by meaning, base its answers on what it found, and be configurable for each event.</p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Architecture" title="From ingestion to chat and analytics">
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.architecture)} aria-label="XPO chatbot data flow">
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Ingestion</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Python and Scrapy</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Collect and clean event-site content</span></div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓</div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Retrieval API</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>.NET and Azure OpenAI</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Create embeddings and run semantic search</span></div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓</div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Storage</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Cosmos DB</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Store event documents, profiles, sessions, and analytics</span></div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓</div>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Experience</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Chat widget and Next.js dashboard</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Answer visitors and show how the system is being used</span></div>
    </div>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Contribution" title="From source website to answer">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Worked on the Python pipeline that scrapes and cleans several event websites.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Built and refined .NET endpoints for embeddings, semantic search, chat, authentication, registration, and analytics.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Connected Azure OpenAI and Cosmos DB, including retries for bulk uploads that hit rate limits.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Added prompts per event, stand-number handling in several languages, input sanitization, rate limiting, and frontend behavior that can be configured.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Worked on the production deployment configuration, better logging, the CORS setup, and the flow behind the analytics dashboard.</li>
    </ul>
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.links)}><a {...stylex.attrs(portfolioStyles.link, caseStudyStyles.importantLink)} href="https://github.com/SnaetWarre/Industry-Project-Xpo-Group">View repository ↗</a></div>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Result" title="One backend for several events">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>The finished app served several events' datasets and bot configurations from the same retrieval service. Each event's content could be scraped, embedded, queried through the chatbot, and followed through registration and analytics, without a separate backend for every event.</p>
  </CaseSection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
